//? Title: Consistency Models: Boundary Maps, Teachers and EMA Targets
//? Subtitle: Native tensor components with editable training and sampling loops
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
This report preserves the original consistency_model experiment and moves reusable tensor operations into datamunge. Parameter stores, objectives, minibatch loops, optimizer writes and sampling trajectories are visible in the complete program.
)
\toc

> Method, preserved protocol and observed limitations

[Song, Dhariwal, Chen and Sutskever, Consistency Models (2023)](https://arxiv.org/abs/2303.01469) motivates a map constant along probability-flow paths. This two-dimensional Gaussian fixture uses separate1474-value online and EMA-target MLPs. With shift=t-.01f, c_skip=.25/(shift²+.25) and c_out=.5*shift/sqrt(.25+t²), the map is c_skip*x+c_out*F. It is exactly the identity at its source-rounded boundary.

The caller explicitly initializes the target from online leaves, constructs Gaussian perturbations and an analytic-Gaussian Euler teacher, and minimizes online-to-**stop-gradient target** MSE. There are48 Adam writes over three epochs. Each write is followed by a separate source-rounded EMA:target=.1f*online+(1.f-.1f)*target. Target gradients are checked absent; no optimizer or EMA is hidden in the native map.

Test consistency MSE is 0.000347818073. Oracle-endpoint MSE is 0.108466069 versus 0.732219597 for identity. These are different objectives:small consistency residual alone does not prove exact endpoints or a correct generated distribution. The source's one-step/multistep samples and analytic-prior control remain visible.

> Follow the state through one model operation

The method diagram separates the explicitly supplied state and conditioning from the predictor and the single transition. The caller owns repeated transitions and training.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/consistency_model_method.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main(){std::filesystem::create_directories("build");dm::graphics::Diagram d(28,1150);dm::graphics::DiagramNodeStyle s;s.width=11;s.height=5;s.font_size=30;d.node("input",{-18,0},"Noisy x,y + t\nGaussian teacher",s).node("predict",{-5,0},"Online / target\nBoundary maps",s).node("step",{8,0},"Stopped target loss\nExplicit gradients",s).node("loop",{21,0},"Adam then EMA\nCaller owns writes",s).edge("input","predict").edge("predict","step").edge("step","loop").save_svg("build/consistency_model_method.svg");}
