> Trace the executed predictor

This graph comes from the actual native compact predictor with 1474 parameter values in six leaves. The input is the encoded feature vector; the experiment below shows its state, time and condition construction.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/consistency_model_network.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main(){namespace n=dm::nn;namespace m=n::models;std::filesystem::create_directories("build");n::ParameterStore p(19003);m::InitializeDiffusionMlp(p,10,2);
 n::Module model([&](const n::Tensor& encoded){auto path=m::DiffusionMlp(p,encoded);n::model_stage("Hidden1:32 SiLU",encoded,path.hidden1);n::model_stage("Hidden2:32 SiLU",path.hidden1,path.hidden2);return n::model_stage("Prediction:2 coordinates",path.hidden2,path.value);},"Executed compact predictor:1474 values / six leaves");
 n::ModelPlotOptions options;options.detail=n::ModelPlotDetail::Blocks;options.sizing.minimum_extent=2;options.sizing.max_planes=2;auto figure=model.plot(n::zeros({1,10}),options);if(figure.parameter_count()!=1474||p.count()!=1474||p.size()!=6)throw std::runtime_error("Predictor census");figure.save_svg("build/consistency_model_network.svg");
}
